Make platformio_project able to build and upload with a Bazel-provided
PlatformIO binary.

Upstream, the build and upload actions resolve `platformio` from a hard-coded
PATH (`/bin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin`), which forces the tool to
be installed out-of-band on the host (e.g. a symlink in /usr/local/bin pointing
at a virtualenv). This adds an optional `platformio` attribute; when set, the
build action invokes that executable instead, and the generated `bazel run`
upload script invokes it from the runfiles tree. This allows a hermetic,
Bazel-managed PlatformIO (see //starlark/platformio:platformio).

--- platformio/platformio.bzl
+++ platformio/platformio.bzl
@@ -256,16 +256,24 @@
+  if ctx.attr.platformio:
+    build_command = "%s run -s -d %s" % (ctx.executable.platformio.path, project_dir)
+    platformio_tools = [ctx.executable.platformio]
+  else:
+    build_command = _BUILD_COMMAND.format(project_dir=project_dir)
+    platformio_tools = []
+
   commands = []
   for zip_file in transitive_zip_files.to_list():
